# A male calling
# What a male does once he is no longer satisfied: he turns slowly back and forth on the
# spot, and his head ring blinks a repeating on/off pattern - his way of saying who he is
# and what he wants. Movement times below are estimates: measure them once and correct
# this file.

0 His head ring lights up bright white and stays on.
0 He starts to turn, swinging towards one end of his travel - about a quarter of a turn from where he was standing.
2 The ring begins to blink: ten steps, one fifth of a second each, so the whole pattern takes two seconds.
2.35 Then the ring goes out and stays out for a little over two seconds. This silence is not a pause between messages, it is part of the message: it marks where the pattern begins and ends, so a female who catches it knows which flash was the first one. Without it every flash could be the first, and she has to guess.
0 The next pattern starts four and a third seconds after the last one did. Stand and watch: two seconds of flashing, two seconds of dark, over and over.
1.5 He reaches the end of his turn and immediately starts turning back the other way. One sweep takes roughly 6 seconds, so he reverses about every 6 seconds, without pause, for as long as he is calling.
0 The pattern itself says two things at once: which male he is (male 1 and male 2 have different patterns) and which appetite he wants satisfied - O, P, or both. Each male has four possible patterns and blinks only one at a time.
143.5 He carries on exactly like this, turning and repeating the same pattern, for the next two and a half minutes.
0 Both his appetites now pass the frustrated mark, and he switches to his "both" pattern. He keeps that same pattern for the rest of the evening, because nothing ever lowers an appetite again.
0 The switch is clean: he picks the pattern once, when a burst starts, so the change waits for the next burst rather than cutting the current one in half. It used to cut it in half, which produced a few seconds of flashes belonging to neither pattern.
0 He never stops calling. There is no moment in the artwork where a male decides he has been answered and goes quiet - once a male starts, he turns and blinks until the whole installation is shut down.
